Error [E1304]: `parse` expects 1 argument (argv), got 2
  --> tests/ui/args_spec_bad_parse_arity.jet:6:20
    |
  6 |     parsed :: spec.parse(io.args(), "extra") ?? panic("parse failed")
    |                    ^^^^^
 Why: `ArgsSpec.parse(argv)` parses a `[String]` (from `io.args()`) against the spec
 Fix: pass exactly one argument: the argv list, e.g. `io.args()`

Error [E0311]: `flag` isn't a method on this value
  --> tests/ui/args_spec_bad_parse_arity.jet:7:18
    |
  7 |     print(parsed.flag("help"))
    |                  ^^^^
 Why: only struct and enum values have instance methods
 Fix: check the spelling of `flag`
